#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0033 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "D4 (PLAN-join-key-type-identity) §4.5 — THE RENDERING PIN. Deliberately NOT a type case: VISITNUM is Num on BOTH sides, so nothing here touches the type axis. KeyMatchRowExpander.tuple used to render every key part through KeyPart.reportingForm(), cleaning a double to 12 SIGNIFICANT DIGITS, so LB.VISITNUM 99.0000000000001 and SV.VISITNUM 99.0000000000002 both cleaned to 99 and the join MATCHED. D4 dropped reportingForm(): PresentNumber now compares EXACTLY and the two STOP JOINING. That half is unchanged and is still what this fixture exists to pin. ⭐⭐ WHAT CHANGED 2026-09-22 (PLAN-unplanned-visit-sv-match-tier): the VERDICT is a violation again, and by a different route. Under D4 alone the unmatched row made SV.SVPRESP read unmatched, the planned-visit condition went false and the rule fell SILENT — this file recorded that silence as the expected answer. That silence WAS the R-7.9 defect: the row was dropped because SV had nothing to say about it, not because the visit was unplanned. The cascade now carries an explicit `not SV._matched_` tier, so an unmatched row falls through to the VISIT-name tier, 'WEEK 99' marks nothing, the visit is treated as planned, 99.0000000000001 is not a TV.VISITNUM and the rule FIRES. ⚠ Same verdict as PRE-D4, opposite mechanism: pre-D4 it fired because the join MATCHED and SVPRESP=Y; now it fires because the join does NOT match and the name tier decides. Do not read a green here as evidence that reportingForm() is back."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VISIT="WEEK 99"
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 99.0000000000001 | WEEK 99
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVPRESP  type=Char label="Pre-Specified"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 99.0000000000002 | WEEK 99 | Y
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 2 | BASELINE
---
